-- title:
--   Far Witt components of the logarithm covector lie in pR
-- statement:
--   Let $\mathcal O$ be a commutative ring and $p$ a prime such that $p$ is a non-zero-divisor in $\mathcal O$, equipped with an $\mathcal O$-algebra structure on $\mathbb Z/p$ whose structure map has kernel exactly $(p)$, and assume $\mathcal O$ is $(p)$-adically complete. Let $F$ be a commutative $d$-dimensional formal group law over $\mathcal O$, i.e. $d$ power series $F_i$ in the variables indexed by $\mathrm{Fin}\,d \sqcup \mathrm{Fin}\,d$ with vanishing constant terms, linear coefficients $\delta_{ij}$ on each side, associative and symmetric under swapping the two groups of variables. Let $F^{(p)}=(Fp_i)$ be power series with vanishing constant terms satisfying $p\cdot\mathrm{coeff}_m(Fp_i)=p^{\deg m}\,\mathrm{coeff}_m(F_i)$ for all $m\neq 0$, that is, the rescaled law $p^{-1}F(pX,pY)$. Let $\varphi=(\varphi_i)$ be $d$ power series in $d$ variables with vanishing constant terms, linear part the identity matrix, coefficients tending to $0$ $p$-adically (for each $N$ and $i$, all but finitely many coefficients lie in $(p^N)$), and additive for the rescaled law: $\varphi_i\circ F^{(p)}=\varphi_i(X)+\varphi_i(Y)$. Let $v\in\mathbb N$ and let $R$ be a commutative ring which is a Hopf algebra over $\mathcal O$, free and finite as an $\mathcal O$-module, with $R$ and $R\otimes_{\mathcal O}R$ both $(p)$-adically complete. Let $\pi:\mathcal O[[X_1,\dots,X_d]]\to R$ be a surjective $\mathcal O$-algebra map such that each $\pi(X_i)$ lies in the radical of $pR$, such that $\pi$ is given by $(p)$-adic evaluation of power series at the points $\pi(X_i)$, such that $\ker\pi$ is generated by the components of the $p^v$-th iterate series $[p^v]_F$ (defined recursively by $[0]_F=0$, $[n+1]_F=F([n]_F,X)$), and such that the comultiplication of $R$ sends $\pi(X_i)$ to the $(p)$-adic evaluation of $F_i$ at the points $\pi(X_j)\otimes 1$ and $1\otimes\pi(X_j)$ in $R\otimes_{\mathcal O}R$. Assume finally that the Cartier dual of $(\mathbb Z/p)\otimes_{\mathcal O}R$, namely the $\mathbb Z/p$-linear dual $\mathrm{Hom}_{\mathbb Z/p}((\mathbb Z/p)\otimes_{\mathcal O}R,\mathbb Z/p)$ with its convolution ring structure, is a local ring. Then there exists $n_0\in\mathbb N$ with the following property: for every $M\in\mathbb N$, every $i$, and every family $c:(\mathrm{Fin}\,d\to_0\mathbb N)\to\mathcal O$ such that $c_m=p^{M-\deg m}\,\mathrm{coeff}_m(\varphi_i)$ whenever $\deg m\le M$, and such that for $\deg m>M$ either $c_m\,p^{\deg m-M}=\mathrm{coeff}_m(\varphi_i)$ or else $c_m=0$ and $p^{\deg m-M}\nmid \mathrm{coeff}_m(\varphi_i)$, and for every Witt vector $\ell\in W_p(\mathcal O[[X_1,\dots,X_d]])$ whose ghost components of index $n<M$ have coefficients $\mathrm{coeff}_{m'}(w_n(\ell))=c_{p^{M-1-n}m'}$, one has $\pi(\ell_{M-1-n})\in pR$ for all $n$ with $n_0\le n<M$.
--
--   This is the point at which unipotence of the special fibre enters: for the finite Hopf algebra $R$ cutting out the $p^v$-torsion of $F$, with unipotent (equivalently, local Cartier dual) reduction mod $p$, the Witt components of the truncated logarithm covector become divisible by $p$ after $\pi$ beyond a bound $n_0$ independent of the truncation length $M$; equivalently, the covector attached to a point of $F[p^v]$ has finite effective length. It feeds the construction of the Witt-vector (Dieudonné/Fontaine covector) map in [`Deformation.truncate_map_mem_wittHom_of_forall_coeff_ghostComponent_eq_logCovector`](thm.html#Deformation.truncate_map_mem_wittHom_of_forall_coeff_ghostComponent_eq_logCovector), and is proved from the nilpotence of the Hasse–Witt matrix of the $p^v$-division series together with the divisibility estimates on the coefficients of $\varphi_i$.
